## Why This Question Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design per-key rate-limiting state, implement TTL-based eviction, ensure idempotence across replays, and align with KCNA consumer semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key sliding or fixed-window counters
- TTL-based eviction and memory safety
- Idempotence with replay handling
- Backpressure and stable commit boundaries

## Code Example
```javascript
class RateStore {
  constructor(ttlMs) {
    this.ttlMs = ttlMs;
    this.store = new Map();
  }
  get(key, minute) {
    return this.store.get(`${key}:${minute}`) ?? 0;
  }
  increment(key, minute) {
    const entry = this.store.get(`${key}:${minute}`) ?? { count: 0, timestamp: Date.now() };
    entry.count++;
    this.store.set(`${key}:${minute}`, entry);
    return entry.count;
  }
  prune() {
    const now = Date.now();
    for (const [key, entry] of this.store.entries()) {
      if (now - entry.timestamp > this.ttlMs) {
        this.store.delete(key);
      }
    }
  }
}

class AlertingSink {
  constructor(limit = 100, windowMs = 60000) {
    this.rateStore = new RateStore(windowMs);
    this.limit = limit;
    this.seenMessages = new Set();
  }
  onMessage(ctx, msg) {
    if (this.seenMessages.has(msg.offset)) return;
    this.seenMessages.add(msg.offset);

    const minute = Math.floor(Date.now() / 60000);
    const count = this.rateStore.increment(msg.key, minute);
    if (count <= this.limit) {
      ctx.emitAlert(msg);
    }
  }
  commitOffsets() {}
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to join across topics with late-arriving updates, implement a TTL-based in-memory state store, and maintain at-least-once semantics while isolating enrichment logic.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-topic enrichment and per-key state
- TTL-based eviction and stale data handling
- Out-of-order arrival tolerance and idempotent processing
- Error routing to dead_letters and offset management

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton: in-memory profile store with TTL
class ProfileStore {
  constructor(ttlMs) { this.ttlMs = ttlMs; this.map = new Map(); }
  update(userId, profile) { this.map.set(userId, { profile, t: Date.now() }); }
  get(userId) {
    const e = this.map.get(userId); if (!e) return null;
    if (Date.now() - e.t > this.ttlMs) { this.map.delete(userId); return null; }
    return e.profile;
  }
}
```

